# promise: #574
# A page's own Print button (window.print(): a boarding pass, an invoice, a recipe) opens Chrome's print
# preview over the page, big enough to use, and the page waits on it. Print preview sized itself to its
# Browser's window, which on the engine is a never-seen 1 pt strip since 0.1.49 (#346): it came out
# 1000 × 3 pt, the button seemed to do nothing and the page waited on a dialog no one could see.
# cra-page-dialogs.patch sizes and places it against the page. Its buttons are a web page's, which the
# readout can't press: the quit at the end closes it. (Cra's File ▸ Print… opens the system panel instead.)
budget rss=900 stalls50=30
pace 0.5
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true}
cra://debug?windowSize=1200x800
cra://open?url=${ORIGIN}/dialogs.html?n=print
expect-log GET /dialogs.html\?n=print
wait 2
cra://debug?cdp=Runtime.evaluate&params={"expression":"(setTimeout(()=>{print();said.push('printed')},0),'print asked')","userGesture":true}
expect-log "value":"print asked"
wait 4
cra://debug?pageDialogs=print
expect-log page dialog print: chrome [0-9]{3,}x[0-9]{3,} at=page front=1
reject-log page dialog print: .* at=sliver
reject-log fault:
